    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0513" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg501"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/325: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Marseille</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Marseille</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-03T10:00:00+00:00">April 3, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 3—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s April 2, 7 p.m.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d442-f1"/> Prisoners charged
                    with violation of French law of January 21, 1937, and the ministerial decree of
                    February 18, 1937,<anchor n="55" xml:id="d442-f2"/> by having passed in transit
                    through French territory en route to Spain in order to enroll in the forces
                    fighting there. The French press states that prisoners have now admitted to the
                    French authorities that this was their intention. Full report by mail.<anchor
                        n="56" xml:id="d442-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d442-f1" n="54" xml:id="d442-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it instructed the Consul General to cable charges on which prisoners
                    were held (852.2221/317).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d442-f2" n="55" xml:id="d442-f2-content">
                <p>See telegrams No. 89, January 22, 2 p.m., and No. 242, February 19, 1 p.m., from
                    the Ambassador in France, <ref target="#pg231">pp. 231</ref> and <ref
                        target="#pg479">479</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d442-f3" n="56" xml:id="d442-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
